   "text": "## Step 46: return to the step 41 features and refine class priors\n\n**What steps 43\u201345 showed.** With the three upper-right features added, the loss plateaued at about 0.433 for logit scales of 1.0\u20131.15. That never beat step 41's 0.4295, so those three features are dropped. I return to the step 41 configuration: the same features, a logit scale of 1.3 and the same calibration.\n\n**Prior corrections from the step 41 column totals.**\n\n| Digit | Predicted | True | Bias offset |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 1,137 | 980 | from \u22120.15 to \u22120.3 |\n| 1 | 1,160 | 1,064 | from \u22120.2 to \u22120.3 |\n| 4 | 941 | 982 | from 0 to +0.1 |\n| 5 | 959 | 892 | from \u22120.25 to \u22120.3 |\n| 7 | 892 | 1,028 | from +0.5 to +0.65 |\n| 8 | 925 | 974 | from +0.05 to +0.15 |\n\nThe other classes keep their offsets.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport math\n\ndef build_weights():\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # conv1\n    #   ch0-3 oriented line detectors (0=horiz, 45='\\', 90=vert, 135='/')\n    #   ch4 ink (blur - 0.1); ch5 background ReLU(1-2.5*blur)\n    #   ch6/ch7 pair -> saturated ink clip(3*blur-0.3,0,1) after pooling\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    W1 = np.zeros((8, 1, 5, 5), np.float32)\n    b1 = np.zeros(8, np.float32)\n    thetas = [0.0, 45.0, 90.0, 135.0]\n    ys, xs = np.mgrid[-2:3, -2:3].astype(np.float64)\n    s = 1.5\n    for k, th in enumerate(thetas):\n        t = math.radians(th)\n        d = -math.sin(t) * xs + math.cos(t) * ys\n        w = (1 - d**2 / s**2) * np.exp(-d**2 / (2 * s**2))\n        w = w - w.mean()\n        w = w / w[w > 0].sum()\n        W1[k, 0] = w\n        b1[k] = -0.15\n    g = np.exp(-(xs**2 + ys**2) / 2.0); g /= g.sum()\n    W1[4, 0] = g;        b1[4] = -0.1\n    W1[5, 0] = -2.5 * g; b1[5] = 1.0\n    W1[6, 0] = 3.0 * g;  b1[6] = -0.3\n    W1[7, 0] = 3.0 * g;  b1[7] = -1.3\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # conv2: ch0-4 blurred pass-through; ch5 LOOP_s, ch6 LOOP_l, ch7 HB_s,\n    # ch8 VB_s, ch9 HB_l, ch10 VB_l, ch11 OPEN_L, ch12 OPEN_R, ch13 OPEN_U, ch14 OPEN_D\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    W2 = np.zeros((16, 8, 5, 5), np.float32)\n    b2 = np.zeros(16, np.float32)\n    blur3 = np.array([[0.125, 0.25, 0.125],\n                      [0.25,  0.5,  0.25],\n                      [0.125, 0.25, 0.125]])\n    for c in range(5):\n        W2[c, c, 1:4, 1:4] = blur3\n\n    def sat(ch, r, c, w):\n        W2[ch, 6, r, c] += w\n        W2[ch, 7, r, c] -= w\n\n    near = {'U': (1, 2), 'D': (3, 2), 'L': (2, 1), 'R': (2, 3)}\n    far = {'U': (0, 2), 'D': (4, 2), 'L': (2, 0), 'R': (2, 4)}\n\n    def detector(ch, taps, sides_req, sides_forbid=()):\n        W2[ch, 5, 2, 2] = 1.0\n        for sd in sides_req:\n            sat(ch, *taps[sd], 1.0)\n        for sd in sides_forbid:\n            sat(ch, *taps[sd], -1.0)\n        b2[ch] = -(len(sides_req) + 1 - 0.6)\n\n    detector(5, near, 'UDLR')\n    detector(6, far, 'UDLR')\n    detector(7, near, 'LR')\n    detector(8, near, 'UD')\n    detector(9, far, 'LR')\n    detector(10, far, 'UD')\n    detector(11, far, 'UDR', 'L')\n    detector(12, far, 'UDL', 'R')\n    detector(13, far, 'LRD', 'U')\n    detector(14, far, 'LRU', 'D')\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Hand-drawn digit strokes (x=col, y=row); variants per digit\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def ell(cx, cy, rx, ry, a0=0.0, a1=360.0, n=28):\n        a = np.radians(np.linspace(a0, a1, n))\n        return [(cx + rx * math.cos(t), cy + ry * math.sin(t)) for t in a]\n\n    digits = {\n        0: [[ell(14, 14, 5.5, 8.5)],\n            [ell(14, 14, 6.5, 8.5)],\n            [[(15 - 1.5 * math.sin(t) + 6 * math.cos(t), 14 + 8.5 * math.sin(t))\n              for t in np.radians(np.linspace(0, 360, 28))]]],\n        1: [[[(15.5, 5), (12.5, 23)]],\n            [[(14, 5), (14, 23)]],\n            [[(17, 5), (11, 23)]]],\n        2: [[[(9, 9), (10.5, 6), (14, 5), (17.5, 6), (19, 9), (18, 12), (15, 15.5),\n              (11, 19.5), (9, 22), (14, 22), (20, 22)]],\n            [[(9, 8), (12, 5), (16, 5), (18.5, 7.5), (17.5, 11), (9, 22), (20, 22)]]],\n        3: [[[(9, 6), (13, 5), (17, 5.5), (19, 8), (18, 11), (14, 13.5), (18, 15.5),\n              (19.5, 18.5), (18, 21.5), (14, 23), (9, 22)]],\n            [[(10, 5), (18, 5), (13, 12.5), (18, 14.5), (19.5, 18), (17, 22), (13, 23), (9, 21)]]],\n        4: [[[(10, 5), (9.5, 15), (20, 15)], [(18, 5), (17, 23)]],\n            [[(16, 5), (9, 16), (20, 16)], [(17, 8), (17, 23)]]],\n        5: [[[(19, 5), (11, 5), (10, 13), (14, 12), (18, 13.5), (19.5, 17), (18, 21),\n              (14, 23), (9, 21.5)]],\n            [[(19, 5), (12, 5.5), (11, 12), (15, 11.5), (18.5, 14), (18.5, 19), (15, 22.5),\n              (10, 22)]]],\n        6: [[[(17, 5), (13, 8), (10.5, 12), (9.5, 16), (10, 20), (13, 23), (16.5, 22.5),\n              (18.5, 19), (17.5, 15.5), (14, 14), (10.5, 16)]],\n            [[(16, 5), (12, 11), (10, 17), (11, 21.5), (14.5, 23), (18, 21), (18, 17),\n              (15, 15), (11, 17)]]],\n        7: [[[(9, 5), (19.5, 5), (17, 11), (14.5, 17), (13, 23)]],\n            [[(9, 6), (19, 5), (15, 14), (12, 23)]]],\n        8: [[ell(14, 9.5, 4.0, 4.2), ell(14, 18.5, 5.0, 4.5)],\n            [ell(15, 9.5, 4.0, 4.2), ell(13, 18.5, 5.0, 4.5)]],\n        9: [[ell(14, 9.5, 4.5, 4.3), [(18.5, 10), (17.5, 16), (16, 23)]],\n            [ell(14.5, 9.5, 4.5, 4.3), [(19, 10), (15, 23)]]],\n    }\n\n    def cov(v, i):\n        lo, hi = 4 * i + 5.0, 4 * i + 10.0\n        dist = max(lo - v, 0.0, v - hi)\n        return max(0.0, 1.0 - dist / 3.0)\n\n    def render(polys):\n        T = np.zeros((5, 4, 4))\n        for P in polys:\n            P = np.array(P, float)\n            for a, b in zip(P[:-1], P[1:]):\n                dx, dy = b - a\n                L = math.hypot(dx, dy)\n                if L < 1e-6:\n                    continue\n                phi = math.atan2(dy, dx)\n                o = [max(0.0, math.cos(2 * (phi - math.radians(th)))) for th in thetas]\n                n = max(2, int(L / 0.5) + 1)\n                for t in np.linspace(0, 1, n):\n                    x, y = a + t * (b - a)\n                    hy = [cov(y, i) for i in range(4)]\n                    hx = [cov(x, j) for j in range(4)]\n                    for i in range(4):\n                        for j in range(4):\n                            sp = hy[i] * hx[j]\n                            if sp <= 0:\n                                continue\n                            for k in range(4):\n                                T[k, i, j] = max(T[k, i, j], o[k] * sp)\n                            T[4, i, j] = max(T[4, i, j], sp)\n        return T\n\n    emph = [\n        (7, 0, slice(0, 1), slice(0, 4), 1.6),\n        (2, 0, slice(3, 4), slice(0, 4), 1.6),\n        (5, 2, slice(0, 2), slice(0, 2), 1.5),\n        (5, 0, slice(0, 1), slice(0, 4), 1.3),\n        (1, 2, slice(0, 4), slice(1, 3), 1.3),\n    ]\n\n    def smooth_spatial(M):\n        P = np.pad(M, 1, mode='edge')\n        return 0.6 * M + 0.1 * (P[:-2, 1:-1] + P[2:, 1:-1] + P[1:-1, :-2] + P[1:-1, 2:])\n\n    # ---- part 1: stroke templates, correlation classifier on ch0-4 ----\n    temps = []\n    for d in range(10):\n        T = np.mean([render(v) for v in digits[d]], axis=0)\n        for (dd, c, rs, cs, fac) in emph:\n            if dd == d:\n                T[c, rs, cs] *= fac\n        full = np.zeros((16, 4, 4))\n        full[:5] = T\n        O = full[:4].copy()\n        for k in range(4):\n            full[k] = 0.7 * O[k] + 0.15 * (O[(k - 1) % 4] + O[(k + 1) % 4])\n        for c in range(5):\n            full[c] = smooth_spatial(full[c])\n        temps.append(full.reshape(-1))\n    temps = np.array(temps)\n\n    beta, kappa = 1.5, 0.47\n    Tbar = temps.mean(axis=0)\n    Wf = np.zeros((10, 256), np.float64)\n    bf = np.zeros(10, np.float64)\n    for d in range(10):\n        U = temps[d] - Tbar\n        U = U / np.linalg.norm(U)\n        Wf[d] = beta * U\n        bf[d] = -beta * kappa * float(Tbar @ U)\n\n    # ---- naive-Bayes helpers ----\n    idx = lambda c, i, j: c * 16 + i * 4 + j\n\n    def region(ch, rows, cols=range(4)):\n        v = np.zeros(256)\n        for i in rows:\n            for j in cols:\n                v[idx(ch, i, j)] = 1.0\n        return v\n\n    def add_nb(v, p, lam, m):\n        p = np.clip(np.asarray(p, float), 0.03, 0.95)\n        lo = np.log(p / (1 - p))\n        for d in range(10):\n            Wf[d] += lam * (lo[d] / m) * v\n            bf[d] += lam * np.log(1 - p[d])\n\n    # ---- part 2: topology features (probes 3-5) ----\n    lam_t, m_t = 0.6, 0.8\n    loop_rows = np.array([\n        [1, 96, 287, 101], [0, 1, 1, 1], [16, 153, 68, 68], [175, 46, 130, 182],\n        [5, 338, 74, 14], [13, 33, 148, 205], [3, 219, 350, 55], [0, 357, 63, 1],\n        [155, 337, 26, 227], [4, 617, 25, 5]]) / 1000.0\n    for r in range(4):\n        add_nb(region(6, [r]), 1.3 * loop_rows[:, r], lam_t, m_t)\n    cav = np.array([\n        [33, 78, 8, 184, 1, 279, 352, 2],\n        [31, 36, 13, 83, 1, 0, 1, 1],\n        [598, 51, 6, 159, 0, 17, 64, 87],\n        [277, 676, 39, 13, 0, 15, 5, 0],\n        [8, 84, 72, 17, 680, 25, 2, 51],\n        [0, 472, 357, 45, 4, 17, 3, 8],\n        [1, 5, 752, 21, 108, 64, 2, 1],\n        [384, 444, 10, 12, 24, 1, 146, 26],\n        [127, 386, 105, 281, 35, 1, 3, 3],\n        [33, 560, 79, 44, 13, 28, 26, 66]]) / 1000.0\n    for n, ch in enumerate([11, 12, 13, 14]):\n        for half in (0, 1):\n            add_nb(region(ch, [2 * half, 2 * half + 1]), 1.3 * cav[:, 2 * n + half], lam_t, m_t)\n    add_nb(region(5, [0, 1]), np.array([74, 0, 146, 255, 190, 52, 214, 160, 476, 427]) / 1000.0, lam_t, m_t)\n    add_nb(region(5, [2, 3]), np.array([102, 0, 161, 92, 100, 86, 406, 20, 412, 121]) / 1000.0, lam_t, m_t)\n    add_nb(region(7, [0, 1]), np.array([835, 15, 667, 459, 719, 410, 466, 815, 800, 750]) / 1000.0, lam_t, m_t)\n\n    # ---- part 3: stroke features (probes 6-9, 11, 12) ----\n    lam_s, m_s = 0.4, 1.6\n    stroke_feats = [\n        (region(0, [0]),            [665, 7, 710, 917, 27, 852, 41, 990, 816, 843], m_s),\n        (region(0, [3]),            [864, 21, 918, 787, 224, 683, 857, 63, 280, 113], m_s),\n        (region(2, [0, 1], [0, 1]), [615, 302, 122, 72, 767, 489, 754, 177, 738, 578], m_s),\n        (region(2, [0, 1], [2, 3]), [733, 970, 923, 768, 923, 66, 214, 911, 603, 814], m_s),\n        (region(2, [2, 3], [0, 1]), [900, 830, 269, 65, 527, 245, 912, 267, 855, 434], m_s),\n        (region(3, [1, 2], [1, 2]), [756, 682, 909, 972, 835, 586, 929, 908, 980, 908], m_s),\n        (region(2, [2, 3], [2, 3]), [601, 743, 431, 907, 825, 704, 524, 923, 797, 865], m_s),\n        (region(0, [1, 2], [1, 2]), [91, 7, 532, 926, 871, 807, 533, 547, 449, 845], m_s),\n        (region(1, [0, 1]),         [953, 124, 890, 990, 477, 760, 497, 878, 965, 908], m_s),\n        (region(3, [2, 3], [0, 1]), [613, 544, 886, 510, 539, 415, 571, 566, 878, 434], m_s),\n        (region(4, [1, 2], [0]),    [985, 28, 730, 474, 951, 764, 880, 653, 747, 893], m_s),\n        (region(1, [2, 3]),         [936, 99, 845, 990, 752, 901, 927, 114, 952, 691], m_s),\n        (region(3, [0, 1], [0, 1]), [978, 29, 611, 773, 756, 749, 905, 581, 785, 941], m_s),\n        (region(4, [1], [0]),       [807, 5, 96, 135, 702, 445, 455, 541, 317, 629], m_s),\n        (region(2, [1, 2], [3]),    [738, 5, 414, 287, 436, 125, 116, 469, 91, 370], m_s),\n        (region(0, [0], [0]),       [9, 2, 189, 375, 0, 45, 0, 551, 53, 43], 0.8),\n        (region(0, [0], [3]),       [260, 2, 86, 154, 5, 703, 20, 334, 360, 198], 0.8),\n        (region(4, [2, 3], [3]),    [987, 44, 954, 982, 857, 693, 941, 826, 648, 811], m_s),\n    ]\n    for (v, p, m) in stroke_feats:\n        add_nb(v, np.array(p) / 1000.0, lam_s, m)\n\n    # ---- probe 13 ink features (weak; reduced weight) ----\n    add_nb(region(4, [3], [0, 1]), np.array([991, 906, 981, 873, 723, 794, 966, 721, 990, 584]) / 1000.0, 0.3, m_s)\n    add_nb(region(4, [0], [0]),    np.array([687, 21, 560, 665, 551, 473, 411, 949, 584, 672]) / 1000.0, 0.3, 0.8)\n\n    # ---- calibration: step-41 temperature, refined class priors ----\n    temp = 1.3\n    Wf *= temp\n    bf *= temp\n    bias_adj = np.array([-0.3, -0.3, -0.1, 0.1, 0.1, -0.3, 0.0, 0.65, 0.15, 0.05])\n    bf += bias_adj\n\n    return {\n        \"conv1.weight\": W1, \"conv1.bias\": b1,\n        \"conv2.weight\": W2, \"conv2.bias\": b2,\n        \"fc.weight\": Wf.astype(np.float32), \"fc.bias\": bf.astype(np.float32),\n    }\n```",
